  "body_html": "<h1>Balanced Coalitional Game</h1>\n<p>A coalitional game is <strong>balanced</strong> if every balanced collection of\ncoalitions satisfies the weighted worth inequality\n$$\n  \\sum_{S \\in \\mathcal{D}} \\delta_S v(S) \\le v(N),\n$$\nwhenever the positive weights $\\delta_S$ cover each player with total\nweight one.</p>\n<p>Intuitively, if a fractional schedule of coalitions uses each player once\nin total, then the weighted value of that schedule cannot exceed the worth\nof the grand coalition.</p>\n<h2>References</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>[MSZ Ch.17, Thm 17.14] Maschler, Solan, Zamir, <em>Game Theory</em>. Balancedness condition in the\n  Bondareva-Shapley theorem.</li>\n</ul>",
